[
  {
    "retain": 0
  },
  {
    "insert": "Feedback on Your Exposé",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "huge",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "I have added tags to all of my annotations. To simplify locating the text positions to which I refer in my feedback, I referenced the relevant tags with the # symbol in each feedback subheading.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Summary",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "huge",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "This work investigates the effectiveness of Large Language Models (LLMs) for language learning, aiming to address challenges such as teacher shortages and personalization. It emphasizes that LLMs must adapt their teaching strategies to varying difficulty levels to effectively match student proficiency and provide personalized learning assistance. The work plans to evaluate different prompting techniques on current LLM models to identify suitable solutions that provide learners with assistance that is both helpful and appropriately challenging.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Strengths",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "huge",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Possible Issues (#possible issues)",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "large",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Thinking about possible challenges and how to overcome them is an important goal when planning for any type of project as arising issues can endanger the success of the project. For your bachelor thesis in particular, you have to address possible issues before they may arise in order to prevent exceeding your time frame and therefore risk failing your academic degree.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "You mentioned that you want to prepare for possible unavailability of participants by choosing slightly more participants than you expect to require for significant results. You identified the lack of objective metrics in the interviews as a possible issue and suggested using interview guidelines to overcome this issue.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Research Questions (#rq)",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "large",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "A goal when writing an Exposé is to define precise Research Questions (RQ) that clearly reflect which aspects of the research problem, you identified during literature review, should be examined by your methodology. Research questions must allow for complex answers to your research problem, while being focused on examining specific aspects of it.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Your research question precisely captures the introduced topic, while being open ended and allowing for complex answers. Your Sub RQs are mostly open ended and all of them contribute to the main RQ.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "However, I found two minor details that you can improve:",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Sub-RQ1 is a yes/no question. It can be rephrased to \"To what extent can LLMs [...]\" in order to allow for more complex answers.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Since the term \"accuracy of the difficulty\" in Sub-RQ3 was not defined, it is open for interpretation and therefore misses clarity. Instead a clear and easy-to-understand term should be used, e.g., \"coherence between provided and desired difficulty\".",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "When formulating research questions, make sure that they use previously introduced terminology and allow for complex answers, while staying in scope and focusing on specific aspects of the research topic. You can use the slides of lecture 7 for guidance.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Supported claims with relevant sources (#claim, #sources)",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "large",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "The goal of the literature review you have to do before writing scientific work, is to find relevant trustworthy sources you can build up on to identify your research gap. These sources have to be correctly cited to support the research gap you identified and your argumentation about its relevance and the adequacy of the methods you introduce to research it. One goal of this course in particular was to work and correctly use LaTeX templates as training for writing your bachelor thesis with one. To accomplish this goal you should use the provided LaTeX commands for citing and styling text.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "You have cited appropriate, recent sources to support all claims you stated. Most of your sources are well established, often cited scientific works. You cited the sources right at your claims with the provided LaTeX commands.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "There is still room for improvement to further substantiate the correctness of your claims:",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "You cited a pre-print version of 3 sources that are already available as journal paper. Published papers should always be favored over their arXiv pre-prints as they are peer-reviewed.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Your first source is a term paper of a student and thus might not have the required quality as a source for your scientific work. I found the course description at https://cs4760.csl.mtu.edu/2024/ where the project of the author including your cited paper, and a video presentation can be found. You should cite this paper and find more credible sources for claims you based on it.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Your bibliography uses different citation styles: For one citation you only use the DOI, for some citations you use the arXiv Number and URL, and for some the DOI and URL.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Some of your citations miss information, e.g., journal title, thus they are printed in an incomplete way. Either check for and add all relevant metadata, or use a citation style that reflects the metadata you have collected. Your citation should not have placeholders for incomplete information printed.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "If you find a paper on arXiv that you like to cite, you should always evaluate, e.g., on Google Scholar, if the paper was already published. By citing the published version of a paper, your claims are based on a reviewed and revised scientific work, which strengthens them. You should always check the credibility of your sources e.g., with checking the author on Google Scholar or by checking the amount of times a source was cited. ",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Weaknesses",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "huge",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Methodology (#framework, #methodology)",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "large",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "The goal of a methodology section is to provide methods that are aligned with a suitable theoretical framework and tailored to answer all aspects of your research questions. In this context the goal of finding suitable methods for your Exposé was to give you insights into scientific methods and theories used in the research area of your topic, contributing to gaining self-assurance in scientific work. You should use a theory that provides a foundation to answer your research questions and aligns with your methodology. You should describe the research methodology in detail and use well established methods and materials such as standard questionnaires.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "You have briefly discussed your methodological approach, but you should decide on an actual HCI theory, reflect on which methods you want to use to test the theory, and describe these in more detail:",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "HCI itself is not a framework, but a field of study that has resulted in multiple theoretical frameworks (e.g., the interaction framework) that can be used to design the interaction between humans and computer systems. You should clarify this to not confuse the reader. Additionally you should decide on an actual HCI framework or theory that you want to use. This will provide a solid basis to align your methodologies with, in order to answer your research question.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "You have described that the quality of assistance in the dimensions helpfulness and accuracy relative to the required difficulty should be assessed. But you have not described the exact methods to assess it. You need to describe how data is assessed (interviews, questionnaires, logs, ...) and how it is evaluated (pattern recognition, statistical analysis, ...). Semi-structured interviews, through which the quality could be assessed but also other insights could be found, might be suitable for your work. To strengthen the significance and reproducibility of your findings, you may want to use a (standard) questionnaire for quality evaluation.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "As an interview based self estimation of language proficiency can be very prone to error due to psychological factors, this estimation should not be done via self-assessment. You could use interviews with language teachers that estimate the proficiency (qualitative) or a short language quiz (quantitative) instead.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "There is a risk that providing guidelines alone does not reduce subjectivity of the evaluation to an acceptable degree. You should come up with a robust theory that introduces applicable and objective methods to evaluate quality of assistance.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "To find a suitable theoretical framework for the HCI aspect for your work, you can try to search for frameworks on Google Scholar. You should decide on well established frameworks that were frequently cited and researched as this helps you with creating meaningful and reproducible additions to scientific research.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "If you want to assess the human computer interaction with AIs within virtual environments you can search for \"hci ai interaction framework for analysis\". With this search term you can find frameworks like \"AI driven human–computer interaction design framework of virtual environment based on comprehensive semantic data analysis with feature extraction\" by K Li et. al.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Inspecting other research in the same field helps to reflect on your own methodology by comparing methods established scientists have used with your own approaches. Reviewing literature about how other researchers assessed certain properties will help you to find suitable methods to assess these properties yourself. This enables you to clearly describe how exactly you design certain methods, what you plan to assess with them and how this answers your research question.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Schedule (#schedule)",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "large",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Creating a detailed and realistic schedule of all tasks that are required for your work is an important goal, as it enables you to reasonably plan all necessary steps for your bachelor thesis within the given time frame. This should be done by considering all major tasks that are relevant for your work and by organizing them across the given time frame in order to achieve realistic time management.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "I have identified some problems with the order and time budgeting of your schedule:",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "“Designing study scenario”: Designing the study scenario before determining which languages, AI model, and guidelines you're using for your scenario is illogical. First determine which languages and AI model to use. Second, implement the Connection/Interface for the AI model to use. Third, design how to evaluate the assistance quality. Fourth, design the scenario which is a description on how you actually conduct the study (environment, procedure, ...)",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "“Prepare the AI model to be used”: I think 2 weeks of time for the actual AI Connection/Interface Implementation while also recruiting participants at the same time, is insufficient. You may combine the \"Deciding Study Details\" and \"Study Preparation\" Blocks into an \"Implement User study software and scenario\" block and schedule it accordingly with a higher time budget. The “Study Planning” block can be executed in parallel to the recruitment of participants, as this allows for pre-testing and refining of the study scenario with participants recruited early in the process..",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "“Collecting data”: The data was already collected in \"Conducting study\". You should rename this block to “Data Preparation”.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "If you are not sure about how long sub-tasks of your work might take, what they include and how to order them so that they build on each other, you should ask your supervisor to give you some guidance with estimations on task duration, and how to sort them, based on their previous experience.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Support of your Research Gap in the SOTA (#sota)",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "large",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "The goal of conducting a literature review and writing a SOTA section was to learn how to find relevant research gaps by combining recent scientific literature to gain a broad in-depth picture of a specific research field. In the SOTA, you have to clearly state what has been achieved in your particular research field and what relevant aspects of that research remain to be explored. You have to cite sufficient evidence for all of your claims.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Your SOTA section has two issues that need to be resolved:",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "You state that ",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "research on LLM-based personalized assistance in language learning does not focus on adjusting difficulty in learning. You support this research gap only with a single source that is just an implementation example. ",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "#ffffff"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "You cannot use a single implementation to quantify an entire research field. This is not enough evidence to support that your stated research gap actually reflects the SOTA.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "In your SOTA you wrote “Using LLMs to provide personalised assistance in language learning has been also studied [...] since this study has been done using models based on GPT-3, utilizing more recent LLMs can improve on the results, making them more relevant for today’s application\"",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "In the current version that passage reads as if you’re stating the whole research field only used GPT-3, which is not true. If you are referring to the cited master thesis by mentioning “this study” you should clarify that you’re writing about this one example.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "You should either cite a survey paper or add a set of other implementation examples to strengthen your argument for the existence and relevance of the research gap.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "To support your argument that most of the recent research used GPT-3 and other obsolete models, you could combine sources 5, 7, 9 and additional survey papers as a basis for argumentation. To find papers to support your claims, you can always search for the specific topic on Google Scholar. A careful selection of search keywords, e.g.,’ llm language education “difficulty adjustment”’, will help you to find sources to evaluate claims about your research gap.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Missing clarity (#clarity)",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "large",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "A goal of writing the Exposé was to train writing concise texts with clarity and developing convincing argumentative flow. To accomplish this goal, you have to write clear text that is easy to comprehend for the addressee and contains convincing arguments without any vague or ambiguous phrasing.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Your Exposé contains some passages that miss clarity, are vague or ambiguous. Please take a look at the weaknesses that I tagged with #clarity for suggestions to improve each of them.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "To reflect the clarity of our work, you can request feedback from friends and colleagues about the comprehensibility of your text and ask them to describe what your work is about. This helps to identify text parts that need more clarity. If it’s hard for you to come up with more plain verbalization, you can search synonyms in an online dictionary or ask generative AI to find more precise vocabulary and phrasing of your ideas.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Others",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "huge",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Scientific tone and readability (#readability, #tenses)",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "large",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "The goal of writing this Exposé was to gain experience in scientific writing in preparation for your bachelor thesis. Writing an Exposé in particular should enable you to gain experience with creating a convincing topic motivation and a well-founded research approach, without actually having to persuade a supervisor. To accomplish the goal of gaining experience in the scientific research, you have to understand the scientific workflow and be able to write readable texts with a formal, neutral scientific tone.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "You should improve the readability of your work and better match the scientific tone that is common in papers and theses:",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "You should avoid using word combinations that can be replaced by a more precise word or phrase for the given context, e.g., “as well as\" -> “and”. This aligns with the formal tone in scientific texts, reduces verbosity, and improves conciseness. To find appropriate words to replace less formal terms, I recommend using a thesaurus, e.g., thesaurus.com. Another way to explore more formal formulations is to ask a generative AI for rephrasing suggestions.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "You used future tense 15 times. In academic work you should always try to use present tense and only use other tenses if present tense makes no sense. Using present tense will often result in a shorter, more readable text. This improves reader engagement and matches the scientific tone.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "You used subjective magnifications, e.g., \"very relevant\". To match the scientific tone, remove these magnifications or support them with an appropriate source.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "You introduced some additional words that don’t add any information to the affected concepts. As this kind of paraphrasing is informal speech, words that don’t add any information should be removed to improve conciseness and match academic tone.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "There are some sentences that have poor readability and therefore are hard to comprehend. I have suggested an adequate rephrasing for all of those. Just check the #readability tagged weaknesses to find them. ",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "In future scientific works, in particular your bachelor thesis, you should reflect if your work is written in a neutral scientific tone. By checking for and avoiding unsupported magnifications, usage of first person and tenses other than the present, you can improve your written scientific work. As writing in English with a scientific tone improves over time and with experience, you can practice by reading scientific papers and by writing short summaries about them. This helps to transfer commonly used phrasing into your word pool. By asking generative AI to highlight phrases that you could improve to better match the scientific tone, you get direct feedback that helps you to reflect on your common errors and evaluate the quality of your tone.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Style (#style, #repetition)",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "large",
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "The goal of satisfying a certain style is to enable you to write works that meet the high standards of scientific research and present you as a professional. To accomplish this goal, your text has to fulfill standardized style properties, in particular consistent choice of language, consistent citation, ascending numbers in citation lists, and the elimination of unnecessary repetition.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Your Exposé has several passages and components that could be improved in terms of style:",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "You used \"personalised\", which is British English several times. At some point you used \"individualized\" which is American English. For writing English text, not only for scientific work, you should decide which variety of English to use and aim for consistency. This helps your text and language skills to be perceived as more professional. ",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Your Bibliography uses different citation styles: For one citation you only use the DOI, for some citations you use the arXiv Number and URL, and for some the DOI and URL. You should either always provide a URL, or always provide a DOI. Using a DOI provides a standard URL with registered metadata that directs you to the actual work.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "When citing multiple sources, make sure to order them with ascending numbers. You may also want to set the \"sorting=none\" option in your bibliography, if you prefer to enumerate your sources based on their appearance in your text instead of alphabetically.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "One of your tables' horizontal lines is incorrectly placed. While all other horizontal lines visualize a month, the line between week 13 and 14 is within month 4. You should move this line up one week.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "You have several repetitions in your text. Avoid these, as they don’t add new information, make the text less concise, and reduce the reader's engagement. Please take a look at the weaknesses that I tagged with #repetition to get a list of all affected passages.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Besides some distinct vocabulary, British English can often be differentiated from American English by words ending in -ise/-ize. The spelling with s is British English, the spelling with z is American English. As I assume you speak German, it is comparable to the difference between German from Germany and Austrian German. The differences are marginal, but if you intermix distinct terms of both languages, your text will lose professional sounding.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "You can use the DOI of scientific works to generate complete citations, using a doi to bibtex lookup like https://doi2bib.org/ . For literature that has no DOI (e.g., Mariane Hedegaard. “The zone of proximal development as basis for instruction), you may want to use https://citationmachine.net/bibtex/ to create sufficient bibtex citations, containing all relevant information about the source, you were able to identify. To find unnecessary repetition, you can use generative AI services and prompt it to highlight repetitions in your text that can be removed to improve readability without harming the argumentative flow.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  }
]